.TH TTYS 5 2026-09-26 "Substrate" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
ttys \- terminal lines for getty
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/ttys
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file
.I /etc/ttys
lists the terminal lines on which
.BR init (8)
starts
.BR getty (8).
Each line holds a terminal and its status, separated by blanks:
.PP
.EX
tty1	on
tty2	off
.EE
.PP
The terminal is a device name under
.I /dev
or a full path.
The status is
.B on
to run a getty on the line or
.B off
not to; any other status is reported on standard error and the line is
not used.
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored.
At most 16 lines are used.
.PP
.B init
reads the file once, after
.I /etc/rc
has run and before it starts the first getty.
If the file does not exist, gettys run on
.IR /dev/tty1 ,
.I /dev/tty2
and
.IR /dev/tty3 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ttys
.SH EXAMPLES
Leave the first console to the graphical login of
.BR sdm (8):
.PP
.EX
tty1	off
tty2	on
tty3	on
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getty (8),
.BR init (8),
.BR sdm (8)
